// qw_hud_ammo_readout — V2_HUD_Active bottom-RIGHT ammo readout
// Interface: #include once into the qw_hud_active composer menuDef body.
//
// Placement (2026-08-16, Eser live review): bottom-RIGHT, right-aligned.
//
// This block spent one revision at the mockup's bottom-CENTRE slot, chasing the
// regions-JSON window at x640 y716. Playing it showed why that is wrong: the
// weapon-select bar also lives at bottom-centre, so the ammo count and the
// carousel ran into each other. Eser: "sag altta ammo ile ilgili bolum olmali o
// yok, onun yerine ortada ammo count ve weapon select bar ile birbirine giriyor.
// normalde saga yasli bir ammo bolumu olmali sag-alt'ta ve oradaki gauge'lar ve
// degerler tam tersine saga yasli olmali."
//
// So the readout goes back to bottom-right, and — unlike the health/armor
// panels, which keep their content left-aligned even on the right side — the
// label and the value are both RIGHT-aligned (textalign 2), growing leftward
// from the screen edge. That is the mirror the panel pair was missing.
//
// The vcompare region for ammo_readout is still anchored to the mockup's centre
// slot, so this placement scores badly there. That is expected and accepted:
// the gate measures agreement with a mockup, and the mockup's own layout
// collides with a widget it does not draw. Playability wins over the artboard.
//
// 🔴 FULL-VIEWPORT LEAF RULE (hud-v2-redesign.md:26 — hard constraint):
// `hudElement` leaf rects do NOT resolve against their container. The .wui
// rect is back-filled straight to screen pixels against the FULL viewport
// (cl_wired_parse.c:1067-1070 WUI_BackfillToScreen: UNIT_NORM -> value *
// vidWidth/vidHeight), and the Clay-resolved x/y/w/h are then DISCARDED by
// the custom-draw adapter (cl_wired_ui_hud_register.c:493-495) — the legacy
// routine reads only its own config.rect. So moving this readout is TWO
// synchronized edits: the CONTAINER offsets AND every leaf rect. Both are
// applied below; the container positions the flow-text caption, and the leaf
// is hand-placed with an independent full-viewport rect to land inside it.
//
// Container: right 1.94vw / bottom 4vh — the same right inset the armor panel
// uses (11.6vw from its own left edge lands on the same margin), sitting above
// the panel row. NO background and NO border: bare text over the arena.
// Tokens: $accent $font_mono $font_sans.
itemDef {
	name "hud_active_ammo_readout"
	type container
	position absolute
	right 1.94vw
	bottom 4vh
	width 11.11vw
	height 5.56vh
	direction column
	alignX end
	grow 0

	// Caption — flow text at the block top, mirroring the mockup's Mono label.
	// Kept on player.weapon.shortname (fed already-uppercased by
	// cg_wired_bridge.c:694-703); the mockup prints the FULL uppercase name, but
	// bg_weaponlist[].name is mixed-case ("Rocket Launcher", bg_misc.c:272) and
	// upper-casing it is a FEEDER change (engine LoC) deliberately out of scope
	// here. Explicit width PERCENT (NOT width FIT) keeps the proven bound-text
	// pattern — a FIT-width bound text node mis-measures into garbled glyphs.
	itemDef { type 0 rect 0 0 11.11vw 1.07vh height FIT width PERCENT 11.11vw bind "player.weapon.shortname" text "WPN" textalign 2 font $font_mono 8 letterspacing 3.2 forecolor $accent decoration visible 1 grow 0 }

	// Value — right-aligned at x0.972 (the 1.94vw inset expressed in normalised
	// full-viewport units, per the leaf rule above), baseline y0.885 to match the
	// health/armor value row. textalign 2 = RIGHT: the digits grow leftward from
	// the edge instead of spilling toward the weapon bar. fontsize 40x46 is the
	// sibling panels' size, so all three bottom readouts now share one scale.
	// The mockup draws a bar and an icon in neither this block nor its own; both
	// leaves stay dropped.
	itemDef { hudElement "statusbar_value" bind "ammo" anchor BOTTOM_RIGHT rect 0.972 0.885 0 0 font $font_sans fontsize 40 46 textalign 2 forecolor $accent decoration visible 1 }
}
